course: dictionary
lesson: 7627
title: Proceed: go on, or make money
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Proceed» is a stiff, formal word. You will meet it in instructions, exams, announcements and safety signs. Most of the time it means to go on, or to move on to the next step.
explain: Look at the clues around it. «Proceed to the exit» tells you to walk towards the exit. «Please proceed with caution» tells you to go on, but carefully. Try swapping in "go on" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Be careful: the same word can also be about money. «All proceeds go to the hospital» means all the money the event makes goes to the hospital. The words around it, like "go to the hospital", tell you which meaning fits.
fact: «Proceed» means to go on or continue, often after a stop.
fact: «Proceed to» means to go or move to a place, or to do the next thing.
fact: «Proceed with caution» means go on, but carefully, because there may be danger.
fact: «The proceeds» of a sale or event are the money it makes. Proceeds is used in the plural.
fact: In old English, «I proceed» meant «I'll carry on». The King in Alice says, «The trial cannot proceed until all the jurymen are back in their proper places».
exercise: «Please proceed with caution.» What does proceed mean here? | Shout loudly | Stop and go home | Lie down and rest | *Go on, but carefully
exercise: A charity bake sale raised £200. «All proceeds go to the hospital.» What are the proceeds? | *The money the sale makes | Plates and cups | The hospital doctors | The cakes that were left over
exercise: Which word could replace proceed in «Proceed to the next question»? | Forget about | Sleep through | Turn back from | *Move on to
test: In «The trial cannot proceed until all the jurymen are back», what does proceed mean? | Stop for ever | Run away | *Go on or continue | Eat lunch
test: In «the proceeds of the school play», what are the proceeds? | *The money the play makes | The actors in the play | The seats in the hall | The script of the play
exam: In the sign «Proceed to the exit», what should you do? | Sit down on the floor | *Walk towards the exit | Stay exactly where you are | Shout for help
